# Dev Notes 53 — Runtime Execute-Action Public Envelope Dispatch v1

**Date:** 2026-06-19  
**Branch:** `runtime-execute-action-public-envelope-dispatch-v1`  
**Status:** Assistant sandbox candidate staged for the declared public raw action-envelope dispatch scope. Sandbox syntax checks, fixture coverage, worker import hygiene, targeted public-envelope dispatch smoke, existing execute-action/nativeWorkerBackend behavior smokes, current contract-chain smokes, and broader mock/static lifecycle/worker regression smokes passed. Direct GitHub branch verification, artifact/package guard after upload, direct GitHub `main` post-merge inspection, and Michael local Windows/MINGW64 real-runtime public raw-envelope dispatch remain future gates.

---

## 1. Purpose

This branch extends the existing execute-action chain upward so public `executeAction(...)` can accept raw Runtime Dev action envelopes for the current built-in route:

```text
text.generate -> nativeWorkerBackend -> native-worker.default
```

The branch preserves the existing descriptor chain:

```text
raw actionEnvelope
  -> Capability Bus action validation
  -> Capability Router route plan
  -> Capability Service plan
  -> Backend Adapter plan
  -> Capability Execution plan
  -> accepted execute-action plan
  -> execute-action orchestration descriptor
  -> existing runExecuteAction(...)
  -> nativeWorkerBackend execution seam
  -> existing parent runtime substrate
```

This is not a second execution path. It is a small public/input dispatch composition seam above the already accepted execute-action behavior seam.

